Experiment 2: Trust Dynamics and Coalition Stability
Simulate repeated interactions with Bayesian trust update (Theorem 4.5). Record time to reach cooperative equilibrium c^*. Hypothesis: higher initial trust accelerates convergence but is not necessary for eventual cooperation.

Experiment 3: Resilience under Random Node Removal
Randomly remove a fraction p \in [0, 0.5] of actors. Recompute the core and record non-emptiness. Hypothesis: redundancy r_k \ge 2 maintains core non-emptiness for moderate p.

Experiment 4: Delay-Induced Autonomy
Introduce Earth–Mars delay \tau_{\text{EM}} \in [0, 3000] s. Record maximum implementable cooperation intensity. Hypothesis: cooperation intensity drops sharply when \tau_{\text{EM}} > h_{\text{survival}}.

