Appendix E: Detailed Proofs for Section 7 (Resilience)

E.1 Hereditary Property of Convexity

We prove that the restriction of a convex game to a sub-coalition is convex. Let (N, v) be convex. For M \subseteq N, define the restricted game (M, v|_M) by v|_M(S) = v(S) for all S \subseteq M. We need to show convexity: for S, T \subseteq M,

v(S) + v(T) \le v(S \cup T) + v(S \cap T).

Since S, T \subseteq M \subseteq N, and the original game is convex, the inequality holds for the original v. But v|_M uses the same values on subsets of M, so the inequality holds for v|_M as well. Thus convexity is preserved. \blacksquare

E.2 Derivation of Probabilistic Survival (Proposition 7.7)

Given r_k actors with capability level at least \kappa_k. Each actor fails independently with probability p_f. Capability k survives if at least one of these r_k actors does not fail. The probability that all r_k actors fail is p_f^{r_k}. Therefore, the probability that at least one remains is 1 - p_f^{r_k}. \blacksquare

