H.7 Capability Redundancy and Probabilistic Survival

```
 Critical capability k requires threshold kappa_k.
 Actors with K_i^k >= kappa_k are "providers" for k.

 Example:
   Capability k: life support
   Providers: Actor A, Actor B, Actor C  (r_k = 3)
   Failure probability per actor: p_f = 0.2

   Survival probability of capability k:
     P(survive) = 1 - p_f^{r_k}
                = 1 - (0.2)^3
                = 1 - 0.008
                = 0.992

 If r_k = 1 (no redundancy):
   P(survive) = 1 - 0.2 = 0.8

 Thus redundancy increases survival probability.
```

